# tag no longer resolves to the commit below.
repo=https://github.com/Dash-Industry-Forum/DASH-IF-Conformance
tag=v3.1.0
commit=bdf0c27a8f198da7a4bf81634bb01faf7c7c3c06
image=sgai-dashif-conformance:v3.1.0

# Upstream publishes no image, so it is built here from the pinned tree. The
# recipe is the one qualabs-video-replacement/tools/dash-conformance uses for
# v3.0.0, with the same two deliberate deviations from upstream's Dockerfile:
#
#   1. GPAC is NOT compiled (upstream runs an unbounded `make -j`). GPAC backs
#      the SEGMENT modules only; the MPD modules do not need it.
#   2. npm assets are not built. They are the web UI; this runs the CLI.
#   3. The base image is pinned to dunglas/frankenphp:1-php8.4 (upstream uses
#      the untagged image, which now ships PHP 8.6 and fails composer.lock).
#
# The build runs on the legacy builder because it is the one that takes
# --memory / --cpu-quota: this host has had a memory incident building
# exactly this kind of image.
#
# What this auditor is for in this project (ADR 0053): the Global Module
# (schematron) and IOP MPD modules over the spec's MPDs. Its XSD module
# validates against DASH5th.xsd (app/Modules/Common/MPD/XSDValidation.php),
# i.e. the 5th edition, so its XSD verdict on 6th-edition documents is
# discarded, and what it flags on ISO's own 6th-edition examples is its
# false-positive baseline.
